@startuml 4-3-line-buffering
' 4-3. A message (text / image) arrives while the session is BUFFERING - the earlier message is still waiting for silence
' Traced from code at dev-rewrite e09d47b (2026-10-11) . box = file . arrow = function calls function
' italic = what that function does to PSQL / Redis
' BUFFERING = session:{id}:state is BUFFERING . one chat job for this session is already queued
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
autonumber

title 4-3. Message arrives while the session is BUFFERING

actor "LINE\n(reporter)" as LINE
participant "controllers/\nline.py" as CTRL
participant "services/\nsession.py" as SESS
participant "workers/\nworker.py" as WORKER
participant "clients/\nredis.py\n(Redis)" as CRD

note over WORKER : this session's chat job was already taken\nrun_chat is inside wait_for_silence

== the new message hits the webhook ==
LINE -> CTRL : POST /webhook/line -> ... -> on_message(event)
ref over CTRL, CRD
  same as 4-1 from user.find_by_line_id through session.buffer(message)
  the message is saved to PSQL (pending), appended to the buffer, last_message_at = now
end ref
CTRL -> SESS : session.start_buffering(current)
SESS -> CRD : set_buffering_if_idle(session_id)\n<i>SET session:{id}:state BUFFERING NX</i>
CRD --> SESS : False
SESS --> CTRL : False
note right of CTRL
  the key already exists (BUFFERING) -> set fails
  job.enqueue_chat is not called - no second chat job
end note
CTRL --> LINE : 200 "OK"

== worker - the same chat job ==
WORKER -> SESS : session.last_message_at(session_id)
SESS -> CRD : get_last_message_at(session_id)
CRD --> SESS : time of the new message
SESS --> WORKER : float
note right of WORKER
  last_message_at moved -> left > 0
  asyncio.sleep(left) again
  SILENCE_SECONDS is counted from the newest message
end note
ref over WORKER, CRD
  silence reached -> same as 4-2 from session.start_processing through session.finish
  read_buffer returns every message (earlier + new) -> one AI call
  one line.reply, using the reply_token of the new message (newest in the buffer)
end ref
@enduml
